WEBVTT

00:00:03.430 --> 00:00:04.900
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:05.880
Wait, what?

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:07.380
I'm by myself?!

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:10.070
At last, my time has come!

00:00:10.070 --> 00:00:11.290
Shugo, shugo!

00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:13.910
Start it off with a Doki! It's Shugo Chara time!

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.650
Today, we're going to pull off the "Great Get Her Grinning Gambit!"

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:19.630
Kusukusu, Amu-chan and Nagi are going all-out!

00:00:19.630 --> 00:00:22.560
Hey, I wanna be involved, too!

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.430
Let's all get along!

00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:26.020
Doki!

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:36.410
Pyon Pyon

00:00:36.410 --> 00:00:37.570
Fumu Fumu

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.480
Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:40.080
Howa Howa

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.280
Kira Kira

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:42.210
Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:42.210 --> 00:00:44.970
What color is your egg?

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.750
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:52.790
Even if you say mean things,

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:56.640
I know you really love me.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:00.310
Even if we fight a lot,

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:03.980
it's just 'cause we're always together.

00:01:04.470 --> 00:01:07.040
Because you believe in me,

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:10.800
I can do anything!

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:17.100
And that's why I unlock my heart!

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:22.810
The person you want to be; things you want to say.

00:01:22.810 --> 00:01:26.470
Important things; things that are true.

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:30.180
Who you are; what you've yet to realize.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.830
Mysterious things; happy things.

00:01:33.830 --> 00:01:38.740
All of these things are inside your egg!

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:42.880
Pyon Pyon

00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:44.030
Fumu Fumu

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:44.970
Yeah! Yeah!

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:46.520
Howa Howa

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:47.730
Kira Kira

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:48.680
Yeah! Yeah!

00:01:48.680 --> 00:01:51.420
What color is your egg?

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:54.230
Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:09.920
Gotcha!

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:11.180
Fabulous!

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:15.720
We finally caught four of them.

00:02:15.720 --> 00:02:17.770
This is still far from enough.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:24.220
We need more X Egg energy to modify Ikuto-kun's violin.

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:27.450
Yeah. This sure is grunt work, though.

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:29.660
It's all in order to find the Embryo.

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:32.070
Chief, there's a signal on the radar!

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.470
Don't let it get away, catch it!

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:35.470
Right!

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:41.930
Rima vs. Nagihiko! The Two are Rivals?

00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:41.930
Episode 62

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:45.310
Today is the day we give the Royal Garden a nice, thorough cleaning!

00:02:42.410 --> 00:02:45.310
Thorough cleaning

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:52.460
Cleaning!

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:53.670
Cleaning!

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:56.100
Cleaning is so much fun!

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.590
Enough, Yaya-chan.

00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:07.810
Let us all work briskly!

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:10.620
Su's a bit different today.

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:13.470
She can be really annoying when it comes to cleaning.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:15.940
You must work, too, Kiseki-chan! {whoa, she calls him "chan"}

00:03:15.940 --> 00:03:18.480
The King does not do such trivial things as clean.

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:19.470
Yeah.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.540
Sparkly, sparkly-dechu.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:25.100
Don't buff it with the same dry cloth you used for the floor!  {Alternatively, but might be losing too much: "Don't polish/buff with what you used on the floor!"}

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:27.220
Such insolence!

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.600
Are you okay, Rima?

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:29.830
Cleaning!

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:32.770
Watch it, Yaya!

00:03:32.770 --> 00:03:34.140
I'm sorry, Amu-chi.

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:42.450
Ever since she joined the Guardians, Rima's laughed a lot more.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:43.670
Isn't that nice?

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:46.350
Now just who supposedly cleaned this?

00:03:46.690 --> 00:03:49.350
There is still so much dust on it.

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:52.230
You must do it <i>again.</i>

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:54.220
Hey!

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.100
This brings back memories!

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:01.110
Everyone sure was young.

00:04:01.110 --> 00:04:04.820
It's only from last year. I don't think we've changed that much.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:06.490
Oh, it's Nadeshiko.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.980
You sure look like her, Nagi-nii.

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:11.870
Well, we're twins, so yeah.

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:14.100
Amu-chi, have you heard from her?

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:14.770
No.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:16.540
Why not? Aren't you best friends?

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:18.740
Best friends.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:23.060
Well, I guess no news is good news, and she's doing well.

00:04:23.060 --> 00:04:25.050
Yeah, that's right!

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:33.000
You've got to be kidding!

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:36.380
That was funny, wasn't it, Rima?

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:37.270
Rima?

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:40.550
Her best friend is Nadeshiko.

00:04:40.550 --> 00:04:42.700
Nagihiko's younger twin sister.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:43.970
Rima!

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.520
A funny face!

00:04:48.120 --> 00:04:49.910
Rima!

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:54.210
Rima?

00:04:56.140 --> 00:04:57.800
Amu-chan, hurry up!

00:04:57.800 --> 00:04:59.770
If you don't hurry, you'll be late again.

00:04:59.770 --> 00:05:02.180
Zip it, I can still make it!

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:03.190
Amu-chan!

00:05:04.890 --> 00:05:06.850
Good morning!

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:08.320
Oh, it's Nagihiko.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:11.300
It's rare for you to get here later than Amu-chan.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:12.760
You think so?

00:05:14.250 --> 00:05:17.520
Rima, you're going to be late.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:19.540
6th Grade: Star Class

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:21.760
And the next page will be Mashiro-san.

00:05:23.290 --> 00:05:24.530
Mashiro-san?

00:05:26.230 --> 00:05:27.930
Mashiro-san!

00:05:27.930 --> 00:05:31.220
Mashiro Rima-san!

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.890
What's the matter with Rima?

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:43.640
Rima is acting weird?

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:47.430
She's not laughing at my jokes.

00:05:47.430 --> 00:05:49.280
What could have happened?

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:52.350
Maybe she got tired of your jokes, Kusukusu?

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:56.210
My funny face is Rima's bedrock, the foundation of her jokes! {To Quark: My only other suggestions would be "My funny face is the foundation of Rima's jokes!" or just "My funny face is Rima's foundation" with "joke" implied. But that might not work.}

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:57.180
We're sorry!

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:11.120
Rima!

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:14.010
Amu.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:16.810
Is something up? You seem kind of down.

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:17.870
Amu-chan!

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:21.060
Nagihiko.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.250
What are you talking about?

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:24.810
Come on, Rima.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:25.700
Perfect.

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.060
They are... They are...

00:06:28.410 --> 00:06:31.010
A scene with just Hinamori Amu-san and Nagihiko-sama!

00:06:31.010 --> 00:06:32.370
It's just too picture perfect!

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.240
Y-You think so?

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:39.210
Rima?

00:06:43.930 --> 00:06:46.320
She is definitely acting strangely today.

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:48.150
You think so, too, Nagihiko?

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:51.300
Rima is feeling down. I'm worried.

00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:53.880
Amu-chan, can't we do anything?

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:56.720
Maybe. Rima likes gags, so...

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:58.370
Of course!

00:06:58.370 --> 00:07:01.800
If we can make Rima laugh, she'll feel better!

00:07:01.800 --> 00:07:03.430
That's a great idea!

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:06.640
The Great Get Her Grinning Gambit!

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.560
Great Get Her Grinning Gambit?

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:11.100
We'll start the plan this Sunday.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:14.150
Until then, we'll whip Amu-chan into shape!

00:07:14.150 --> 00:07:16.140
What? Whip me into shape?

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:19.720
Special training to make Rima feel better!

00:07:19.720 --> 00:07:21.700
We've got a lot of work ahead of us.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:24.720
Great Get Her Grinning Gambit!

00:07:25.010 --> 00:07:29.350
I'm not so sure about this, but if it helps Rima feel better, then...

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:31.680
You should help out, too, Nagihiko!

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:33.130
Me?

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:35.770
But I'm no good at making people laugh.

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:39.700
Besides that, Rima-chan seems really wary of me.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:42.890
Don't say that. Please help!

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:46.310
How could I possibly refuse that?

00:07:52.050 --> 00:07:53.300
Wrong.

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:54.130
How?

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:56.270
Your hand movements were 0.3 seconds off!

00:07:56.270 --> 00:07:57.650
One more time!

00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:01.890
Will this really help Rima feel better?

00:08:01.890 --> 00:08:04.130
This is her favorite joke!

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:06.800
We've gotta make Rima laugh so she feels better!

00:08:09.080 --> 00:08:10.600
Oh yeah, where's Ran and the others?

00:08:10.600 --> 00:08:13.580
They're preparing for the secret plan.

00:08:13.580 --> 00:08:15.720
Secret plan? What's that?

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:17.720
It's a secret.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:23.720
I'm finished.

00:08:23.720 --> 00:08:25.610
Okay, the next one goes here.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.470
Huh? There's more?

00:08:27.470 --> 00:08:29.900
Please give your best effort, Nagihiko-kun!

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:32.350
Okay! Let's all cheer Nagi on!

00:08:32.350 --> 00:08:36.350
Yay, yay! Nagi! You can do it, Nagi!

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.060
Amu.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:48.030
If you're free this Sunday, would you like to hang out? I'll wait for your reply. -Amu

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:57.050
So where should we go first?

00:08:57.050 --> 00:08:58.440
Why is <i>he</i> here?

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:02.000
You didn't say anything about Nagihiko coming in your text.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:05.180
Is that a big deal? It'll be more fun with three people.

00:09:08.150 --> 00:09:09.140
Rima!

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:12.510
Amu-chan, now's the time to reveal the results of your special training!

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:16.100
There don't seem to be too many people around.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:16.760
Rima!

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:19.370
What's wrong with you?

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:20.920
It didn't work.

00:09:20.920 --> 00:09:22.810
Amu-chan, don't give up!

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:29.260
Wrong! She'll never laugh with that timing!

00:09:30.180 --> 00:09:31.320
Amu-chan?

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:33.450
Hey, react to it, Nagi!

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:36.510
Ha-ha-ha, Amu-chan, you're funny.

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:41.090
Are you two secretly plotting something for me?

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:45.640
It's pointless. Such half-baked gags would never work on me.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:49.200
If you want to make me laugh, you've gotta take it seriously!

00:09:49.200 --> 00:09:50.220
Okay!

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:53.130
Doesn't this change everything?

00:09:53.130 --> 00:09:54.640
That's our Rima!

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:58.000
In that case, we'll do whatever it takes to make you burst out laughing!

00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.350
Let's do it!

00:09:59.350 --> 00:10:01.540
<i>I'm</i> the one doing it...

00:10:21.330 --> 00:10:22.590
It's pretty, isn't it?

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:26.930
Amu-chan is pretty, too!

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:33.400
Wait, Rima!

00:10:36.220 --> 00:10:38.530
Here's one for you, Amu-chan.

00:10:38.530 --> 00:10:40.060
Thank you.

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:46.360
Spicy!

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:47.720
Giant Monster Amu-ra Appears!

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:50.220
Super spicy gags are so out.

00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:54.240
No good?

00:10:54.240 --> 00:10:56.180
Don't make light of humor.

00:10:56.180 --> 00:10:59.340
Rima-chan doesn't laugh very easily, does she?

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:01.140
She's a stubborn one, she is.

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:02.450
Rima.

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:05.460
If it's come to this, it's about time for the secret plan.

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:08.100
And this secret plan is...

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:08.940
What?

00:11:08.940 --> 00:11:11.060
To be continued in the second half!

00:11:25.180 --> 00:11:27.180
Nagihiko, where are we going?

00:11:27.180 --> 00:11:29.140
Oh, just...

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:34.750
It was a great success!

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:36.010
What's this?

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:37.680
The secret plan!

00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:39.310
No one told me anything about it.

00:11:42.640 --> 00:11:43.810
Hey!

00:11:49.140 --> 00:11:51.470
Amu's reaction rules!

00:11:52.500 --> 00:11:56.110
You really did great digging all those holes.

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:58.390
But will she be okay?

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:03.370
Jeez, knock it off already.

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:16.930
There's no need to hold back. If you want to laugh, just laugh.

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:21.640
Or can you not let yourself because I'm here?

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:26.180
Amu-chan is doing her best for you, Rima-chan.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:33.310
Don't talk about Amu as if you know everything about her!

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:36.680
You make me so angry.

00:12:38.700 --> 00:12:40.000
Amu-chan!

00:12:41.850 --> 00:12:43.060
Why?

00:12:45.970 --> 00:12:48.090
What's going on?

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:52.510
Nagihiko, aren't we supposed to make her feel better?

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:53.640
Well...

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:57.220
I want to go to your place, Amu.

00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:59.270
My place?

00:13:01.140 --> 00:13:02.620
I want to go, too!

00:13:03.050 --> 00:13:04.640
I guess I don't mind, but...

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:09.130
Isn't this the first time Amu-chan's had friends over?

00:13:09.130 --> 00:13:10.970
You know, I think you're right.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:12.970
I'm home!

00:13:15.850 --> 00:13:21.070
Wow, it's rare for you to bring friends home, Amu-chan.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:22.990
You think so?

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.880
Mister, your hair is so long and shiny!

00:13:25.880 --> 00:13:27.040
Mister?!

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:30.510
Amu-chan brought a boyfriend home with her?!

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:30.530
Boyfriend

00:13:30.510 --> 00:13:32.470
No, this is...

00:13:37.670 --> 00:13:39.030
Good day.

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:40.010
Nadeshiko!

00:13:40.010 --> 00:13:42.850
Oh, she's a girl.

00:13:45.300 --> 00:13:47.350
So this is your room, Amu?

00:13:48.180 --> 00:13:50.300
It's quite cute.

00:13:50.710 --> 00:13:52.120
You think so?

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:54.310
It looks just like a normal girl's room.

00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:58.320
Does she mean it's different from my usual image?

00:13:54.700 --> 00:13:58.320
Normal Girl

00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:01.060
Oh, it's here.

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:03.470
You kept it all this time.

00:14:03.790 --> 00:14:05.390
Of course.

00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:10.140
That was the first time I met you, right?

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:07.280
Matchmaking Charm

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:12.460
That's right.

00:14:13.730 --> 00:14:17.050
Even if you talk about the past, I still don't know anything.

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:19.890
The ball returns!

00:14:19.890 --> 00:14:21.350
Rima!

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:24.320
Trying to tug at people's feelings again, doing that?

00:14:24.320 --> 00:14:26.350
Stop it, you two!

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:28.150
Ta-da!

00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:29.000
A photo album?

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:29.980
She decided herself?

00:14:29.980 --> 00:14:30.820
Gimme.

00:14:32.700 --> 00:14:35.350
Wow, there are a lot of pictures.

00:14:35.350 --> 00:14:37.220
Well, my dad's a photographer.

00:14:35.370 --> 00:14:44.910
She did it! Amu enters kindergarten!

00:14:37.220 --> 00:14:39.880
This is my sister in kindergarten.

00:14:39.880 --> 00:14:42.200
Is the kid next to you a former boyfriend?

00:14:42.200 --> 00:14:44.220
No way, it was just kindergarten!

00:14:44.220 --> 00:14:46.540
Oh, there are different boys in this one.

00:14:46.540 --> 00:14:49.500
So Amu-chan has had varied tastes since she was young.

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:51.030
What do you mean by that?

00:14:51.720 --> 00:14:55.830
This teddy bear. You always have it with you.

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:58.890
No way, it's only now and then, right?

00:14:57.590 --> 00:14:58.890
Ta-da!

00:14:58.890 --> 00:15:00.110
Hey, Ami!

00:15:00.110 --> 00:15:04.530
My sister's loved dat teddy bear since she was wittle.

00:15:05.040 --> 00:15:05.990
Really?

00:15:05.990 --> 00:15:07.230
No, that's...

00:15:07.230 --> 00:15:10.890
When we moved, Mommy twied to throw it away, but she begged to keep it.

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:11.960
Knock it off, Ami!

00:15:11.960 --> 00:15:13.410
Well, that's unexpected.

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:16.890
No, she's got it wrong. It just wasn't the right time to throw it out.

00:15:21.790 --> 00:15:23.430
Snack time!

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:26.850
Oh yeah, I haven't eaten since breakfast.

00:15:26.850 --> 00:15:28.820
Then, should we make something?

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:37.970
And now, we will begin to make Chou a la Creme!

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:40.000
Su's going at it again.

00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.010
Yep, she sure is.

00:15:41.010 --> 00:15:45.030
First, make the base mixture for Chou a la Creme!

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:52.050
I made sweets with Nadeshiko a long time ago, too.

00:15:52.050 --> 00:15:54.470
Come now, Amu-chan, give it a try.

00:15:55.880 --> 00:15:57.320
What the heck is this?

00:15:58.410 --> 00:16:00.130
Shouldn't you Character Change with Su?

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:01.210
Oh yeah!

00:16:01.210 --> 00:16:03.340
No shortcuts!

00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:04.510
We're sorry.

00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:08.360
Continuing, make the cream that goes inside.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:10.200
You can do it, Rima!

00:16:11.390 --> 00:16:14.100
It won't get fluffy. This is boring.

00:16:14.100 --> 00:16:15.760
Will you let me see?

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:20.090
Like this. If you do it this way...

00:16:27.560 --> 00:16:29.760
It's ready!

00:16:30.340 --> 00:16:35.520
The point here is to slowly increase the speed at which you stir the mixture.

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:37.010
Are we a cooking show now?

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:39.510
Let's eat!

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:44.090
These Chou a la Creme we made sure are delicious.

00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:44.910
Yum.

00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:45.830
{oishi}They're good.

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:53.670
If we can collect this many in one go, we should be able to continue our research soon.

00:16:53.670 --> 00:16:55.930
Yeah! Today was a bumper crop!

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:59.120
Chief! Can't we take a little break?

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:01.180
What are you talking about? Let's go!

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:03.680
Wait, dammit!

00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:12.170
You've got to be kidding me.

00:17:13.590 --> 00:17:15.410
What are you doing?!

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:18.640
Today sure was fun, wasn't it?

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:22.980
Yes. I certainly learned a lot about you, Amu-chan.

00:17:22.980 --> 00:17:24.840
How about you, Rima?

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:26.090
All right, I guess.

00:17:26.970 --> 00:17:28.850
This is our last chance!

00:17:28.850 --> 00:17:30.170
You're still going at it?

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:32.470
The Great Get Her Grinning Gambit is not over!

00:17:32.470 --> 00:17:34.470
